A||N||8||fierojp||Fiero w/ Quad 4 - Glowing Exhaust - HELP!||||9||
Z||000000||fierojp||11-08-2001||04:20 PM||||Hi Fiero Friends, <BR>I have recently installed a rebuilt quad 4 into a Fiero. I drove it for the first time around the block and after a couple of minutes took it back to the garage. I looked at the engine and saw a glowing exhaust manifold! BTW, I do not have a complete exhaust system on this yet. I have the manifold and two 12" bendable tailpipes attached to it to move the hot gases out of the engine compartment. (I will get an exhaust as soon as I find out what's wrong right now). <P>So I'm guessing that the timing is way off or the engine is running very lean for some reason. I did NOT get a code 44 from the ECM indicating a lean exhaust. <P>It is possible that the oxygen sensor would read some outside air in addition to the exhaust gases due to the lack of a complete exhaust. I would expect this to cause a rich condition though... Could it be so rich that unburned gas is combusting in the exhuast? I don't recall hearing any serious backfiring going on... <P>A pretty good shop was the last to see inside the timing chain housing. I'm assuming they installed everything correctly in there. Is there a way I could tell for sure that the timing is messed up without taking the housing apart (it would be very hard to do in the Fiero). <P>One other thing- I do not have a knock sensor currently hooked up. The wiring harness I bought did not come with an input. I am planning on adding it in as I know the computer can handle the signal and probably use it well. Other than the knock sensor issue, all sensors are hooked up and properly functioning. <P>I really hope this is something simple. I'm not going to start the engine again until I know what's going on - I don't want to damage it.  Any ideas would be greatly appreciated! Thanks! <P>J.P.<P>Check out pictures at <A HREF="http://www.fierojp.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierojp.com</A>  (click on Q4 Fiero). <P> <BR> <BR> <BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||87GTZ34||11-08-2001||05:35 PM||||JP,<BR>  Welcome to the forum (you only have 2 posts...) and great project!  I've not seen a Quad 4 swap so I won't be an expert here,  but based on my mechanical skills I think your assumptions could be accurate.  My suggestion would be to get your hands on a scanner to check under the hood of the ECM first. My gut feel is that the engine may not be going into closed loop and you are getting extra fuel thru to the exhaust.  (you can also check this in diag mode w/ SES light.) You will need a scanner to help with dialing it in anyway.  If everything checks out there, then you will need to check cam timing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||erikred||11-08-2001||06:00 PM||||If your exhast manifold is glowing, the engine is running rich. Check your fuel pressure. My brother had a bad regulator on has Grand AM and it would just dump gas out the tail pipes. It could also be the Throttle Postition Sensor is out of adjustment or a bad O2 sensor. Make sure you gapped the plugs correctly. It may sound stupid but I gapped mine to little once and the cat started glowing. Run fine for a while though.<P>Erik-||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierojp||11-08-2001||06:43 PM||||Thanks for the replies guys!<P>ErikRed- you think the engine is running rich?  Everywhere I look, it says that with a glowing manifold, you have a lean condition.  But, if you're right, I would bet it is due to the fact that the complete exhaust system is not installed yet.  The oxygen sensor is not far away from outside air.  I don't get any codes from the sensor, so it thinks everything is right.  But, in actuality, the sensor is reading part exhaust gas and part outside air and thus sending more fuel (too much) into the engine.  Maybe???  Any thoughts??  Would a complete exhaust solve the problem?  <P>Thanks!<BR>JP<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||11-08-2001||08:10 PM||||2 things will cause glowing manifolds:<BR>Too lean, exhaust temp WAY too high from combustion, or too rich, with fuel continuing it's burn inside the exhaust system... ||||reg||6
Z||000005||FieroMaster88||11-08-2001||09:34 PM||||I am not sure about the Quad 4, but my manafolds were glowing on my V6 because of a vacuume leak.  You could look into that as well.  Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierojp||11-08-2001||11:13 PM||||So how many people think the engine is running very rich due to the oxygen sensor sensing some outside air?  Maybe completing the exhaust would solve the problem...<P>** I don't believe I have a vacuum leak - all new gaskets, all hoses are good...<P>** I haven't checked the fuel pressure, but I'm assuming everything is good there as well - new V6 fiero fuel pump, new HO Quad 4 injectors, new filter.<P>JP||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||11-09-2001||07:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierojp:<BR><B>So how many people think the engine is running very rich due to the oxygen sensor sensing some outside air?  JP</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I DO I DO!!!!!!!!!<P>Either a Lean, or VERY rich condition, can cause manifold melting...<P>In your case, I'd say your O2 sensor is waaay off due to outside air contamination.<P>Complete the exhaust, with a catalyst and muffler, and then it should run like a champ!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierojp||11-10-2001||02:49 AM||||Allright,<BR>I'm crossing my fingers - I'm gonna take the car to get the custom exhaust made ASAP, then an alignment, and then I'll be in Fiero Heaven with my Quad 4!<P>Thanks,<BR>JP||||reg||1
